{
	"_comment": [
		"chrome.json - seccomp profile for Rover's headless (Chromium) container.",
		"",
		"Derived from Docker's ACTUAL MAINTAINED default seccomp profile:",
		"  github.com/moby/profiles, module seccomp v0.2.3+, file seccomp/default.json",
		"  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moby/profiles/main/seccomp/default.json",
		"  Migrated into that module from moby/moby's profiles/seccomp/default.json",
		"  in moby/moby commit a600da91f47c (2025-07-22, \"profiles/apparmor,",
		"  seccomp: migrate to separate module\"). Generated by seccomp/generate.go,",
		"  whose own comment states its purpose: \"saves the default seccomp",
		"  profile as a json file so people can use it as a base for their own",
		"  custom profiles\" - i.e. this is the intended base for exactly this",
		"  kind of derivation.",
		"",
		"PROVENANCE CORRECTION (round 2 of this file): the first version of this",
		"profile was derived from daemon/pkg/oci/fixtures/default.json in the",
		"moby/moby repo instead of the file above. That fixture was created in",
		"2020 (moby/moby commit c9c77563011f, \"oci: add tests for loading",
		"seccomp profiles\") as a literal, static test input for",
		"TestSeccompLoadProfile - a parser test, never compared against",
		"DefaultProfile() - and its content was never updated after. It was",
		"wrongly treated as Docker's real default profile on weaker evidence",
		"than that: the brief's specified path (profiles/seccomp/default.json)",
		"404'd, a repo-scoped code search for \"seccomp\" surfaced the fixture as",
		"a plausible-looking candidate (filename default.json, path containing",
		"both \"oci\" and \"seccomp\"), and a commit-history lookup on that exact",
		"path returned one commit - c74ba95583051d0d49280d242b3b72bc3e54693d",
		"(2025-07-24, a same-repo package move) - which was misread as proof the",
		"file itself was the historically-shipped default profile under a new",
		"path. Neither the fixture's content nor its lineage was ever diffed",
		"against Docker's actually-generated default profile before relying on",
		"it; the commit-history tool used only follows renames within moby/moby,",
		"so it could not have surfaced (and never was checked against) the real",
		"profile's actual, separate migration: moby/moby commit a600da91f47c",
		"(2025-07-22, two days earlier) moved profiles/seccomp/default.json out",
		"of moby/moby entirely, into a different repository (moby/profiles),",
		"under a non-obvious top-level module path unrelated to daemon/pkg/oci.",
		"Measured impact of that error: the stale fixture was missing 58",
		"syscall names versus the real default (384 vs. 442), had no",
		"defaultErrnoRet, no clone3 deny rule, and critically no argument filter",
		"on `socket` - so the derived profile from round 1 allowed socket(2)",
		"unconditionally, including AF_VSOCK (host<->guest transport) and",
		"AF_ALG (kernel crypto API), both of which upstream deliberately blocks.",
		"That widening is fixed in this version; see the two changes below,",
		"which are the ONLY two changes versus the base cited above.",
		"",
		"Changed relative to that upstream default, and NOTHING else:",
		"",
		"1. clone: upstream allows the namespace-creation flags (CLONE_NEWNS,",
		"   CLONE_NEWUTS, CLONE_NEWIPC, CLONE_NEWUSER, CLONE_NEWPID, CLONE_NEWNET,",
		"   CLONE_NEWCGROUP) only when the caller already has CAP_SYS_ADMIN;",
		"   without it, an argument mask (value 2114060288 / 0x7E020000, both the",
		"   x86 arg-index-0 and s390 arg-index-1 variants) blocks exactly those",
		"   flags. That mask is removed: clone is allowed unconditionally, any",
		"   flags.",
		"",
		"2. unshare / setns: upstream allows these only when the caller has",
		"   CAP_SYS_ADMIN. Rover's headless container runs as uid 10001 with",
		"   Docker's default capability set (no CAP_SYS_ADMIN), so upstream",
		"   denies both outright. They are pulled out of that CAP_SYS_ADMIN gate",
		"   and allowed unconditionally.",
		"",
		"Why: Chrome's namespace sandbox creates an unprivileged user namespace",
		"(CLONE_NEWUSER, via clone or unshare) plus PID/net/mount namespaces",
		"layered on top, all without CAP_SYS_ADMIN on the host. Docker's own",
		"default profile blocks exactly this - verified empirically:",
		"  docker run --rm debian:bookworm-slim sh -c 'unshare --user --map-root-user id'",
		"    -> Operation not permitted",
		"  docker run --rm --security-opt seccomp=unconfined debian:bookworm-slim \\",
		"    sh -c 'unshare --user --map-root-user id'",
		"    -> succeeds",
		"",
		"Everything else stays exactly as restrictive as upstream, including but",
		"not limited to: mount, umount, umount2, sethostname, setdomainname,",
		"quotactl, quotactl_fd, bpf, perf_event_open, fanotify_init,",
		"lookup_dcookie, fsconfig, fsmount, fsopen, fspick, mount_setattr,",
		"move_mount, open_tree, lsm_get_self_attr, lsm_list_modules,",
		"lsm_set_self_attr, and syslog remain gated behind CAP_SYS_ADMIN exactly",
		"as upstream; clone3 keeps upstream's explicit deny rule for non-",
		"CAP_SYS_ADMIN callers untouched; socket's three argument filters",
		"(blocking AF_ALG and AF_VSOCK, allowing everything else) are untouched.",
		"This container is granted no extra capabilities, so all of the",
		"CAP_SYS_ADMIN-gated syscalls above stay denied in practice.",
		"",
		"chromium-sandbox (the SUID helper) is deliberately not installed (see the",
		"Dockerfile) - it does not rescue the default-profile case, it fails",
		"differently at zygote_host:207 - so this profile is the actual fix.",
		"",
		"This field is not part of the OCI/Docker seccomp schema; it is inert",
		"documentation. Docker's loader ignores unrecognized top-level fields -",
		"verified empirically against this exact file (JSON `//` comments are",
		"NOT accepted by Docker's --security-opt seccomp= loader; a top-level",
		"field like this one is)."
	],
